==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|la|ǵʰer}}
Compound of {{m|la|co-}} (see {{m|la|cum}}) and {{m|la|-hors}} (see {{m|la|hortus}})

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cohors}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|cohors|cohortis|f|third}}

# a [[court]]
# a [[farmyard]] or [[enclosure]]
# a [[retinue]]
# a [[circle]] or [[crowd]]
# a [[cohort]]; [[tenth]] part of a [[legion]]
# a [[band]] or [[armed]] [[force]]
# a [[ship]]'s [[crew]]
# a [[bodyguard]]
# a [[military]] unit of 500 men

====Inflection====
{{la-decl-3rd|cohors}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|la|cōrs}}

